# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example environment configuration — copy to `.dev.vars` (NOT `.env`)
#
# Do NOT put real secrets in `.env`: Vite statically inlines every
# `import.meta.env.*` reference at build time, which bakes the literal value
# into `dist/_worker.js` and ships it to Cloudflare. That is exactly how the
# previous MS_CLIENT_SECRET leaked.
#
# For local development with `wrangler pages dev`, copy this file to
# `.dev.vars` (already gitignored). Both files are ignored by Git.
#
# For production, set each value as a Cloudflare Pages secret:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put MS_CLIENT_SECRET
#   npx wrangler pages secret put SESSION_SECRET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Session signing (required) -------------------------------------------
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# Must be at least 32 characters. Rotating this invalidates all sessions.
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-32-character-random-string

# --- Microsoft Entra ID (required for login) -------------------------------
# The secret below was EXPOSED in the deployed bundle and must be rotated in
# Azure Portal: App Registration > Certificates & secrets > New client secret.
# Delete the old secret after deploying the new one.
MS_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-the-rotated-azure-client-secret

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of email domains allowed to sign in.
ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=edelweiss.sch.id
